  "//charts": "Reference tables for the chart sheet, laid out like the standard gojūon charts. LAYOUT ONLY where possible: a grid cell is a kana string (null = gap in the grid) and a flow item is a kana string, and app.js looks the romaji up from the decks below so the two can never disagree. A flow item may instead be {q, a} to carry its own reading — used for the extended katakana, which are reference-only and not in any deck. `type` is \"grid\" (consonant rows × vowel columns) or \"flow\" (a wrapping list).",
